<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip I, Duke of Pomerania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1515–1560</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip I was duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-wolgast">Pomerania-Wolgast</a> from 1532, when the Pomeranian duchy was divided between him and his uncle Barnim IX. He introduced the Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> in 1534 and married Maria of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, sister of the elector John Frederick.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-i-duke-of-pomerania.jpg" alt="Philip I, Duke of Pomerania" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Filip_I_pomorski.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
